//? Title: LeNet-5: Sparse Connections, Learned Pooling and RBF Outputs
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A digit recogniser needs useful image features with few shared weights. LeNet-5 combines
local convolutions, learned subsampling and a fixed-prototype readout. We preserve the original
sparse C3 connections and parameter count, inspect absent-channel derivatives, and show the
complete tensor Adam loop on original MNIST images.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.1_fundamentals/lenet5.cpp`.

> The method

The padded 32×32 input passes C1(6,5×5), learned S2, sparse C3(16,5×5), learned S4,
C5(120,5×5) and F6(84). Every stage uses 1.7159 tanh(2x/3). S2 and S4 sum each 2×2
window, multiply by a learned channel scale and add a bias. C3 stores only the 60 connected
input/output channel pairs from the paper, rather than masking a dense parameter tensor.

$$
\text{parameters}=156+12+1516+32+48120+10164=60000,\qquad
z_k=-\|h-c_k\|^2.
$$
\alttext(The six trainable stages total sixty thousand scalars; each output logit is the negative squared distance from the 84-dimensional feature to a fixed prototype.)

Disconnected C3 inputs have exactly zero derivative for that output map. The fixed 7×12
seven-segment prototypes used here are our own, not the original paper's digit art. Input
pixels pad to 32×32 and map to [-.1,1.175]. Training uses sparse softmax cross entropy on
negative distances with Adam and kernel L2, a modern adaptation rather than reproduction of
the paper's loss and optimiser. The report exposes three epochs on 256 fitting rows, 128
validation rows and 128 official test rows. Sparse convolution work sums only connected pairs;
parameter sparsity is preserved, while 16 small C3 calls need not minimise runtime.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/lenet5_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/lenet5_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/lenet5_concept.tikz > build/lenet5_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/lenet5_concept.svg build/lenet5_concept.dvi > build/lenet5_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
