> Conclusion

The original sparse architecture has exactly 60000 learned scalars, and absent C3 inputs
have zero derivative. The report distinguishes its fixed prototype art and Adam training
adaptations from the original model and provides a compact executed MNIST demonstration.

> References

- [LeCun et al. (1998), Gradient-Based Learning Applied to Document Recognition](https://doi.org/10.1109/5.726791).
- [MNIST dataset](https://yann.lecun.org/exdb/mnist/).
